    thinking: "**Defining App Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'m zeroing in on defining the application\'s core functions. I\'ve settled on the app name as either \"Kinetic Travel\" or \"Travel Day Companion\". I\'m also updating the metadata with a name and description based on the initial specifications. This forms the essential foundation for subsequent development stages.\n\n\n**Analyzing User Interface**\n\nOkay, I\'m now delving into the user interface components. I\'ve begun visualizing the essential screens, focusing on the profile avatar and the \"Good Morning\" greeting. I\'m exploring a hero card with departure details, including a countdown timer for departure. I am also working through designing smart action cards, with quick action pills for transit options, which can be clicked to open transit options / request rides / view details.\n\n\n**Constructing Departure Timeline**\n\nI\'m now building out the detailed departure timeline. I\'ve fleshed out the events for a departure to SFO, including time-based reminders and interactive elements like a \"View Boarding Pass\" button. I\'m focusing on incorporating real-time information such as weather and baggage drop closure times. I\'m also thinking through how to structure a timeline for the flight arrival.\n\n\n**Designing App Navigation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the app\'s navigation structure. I\'ve designed a bottom navigation bar with \"Timeline\", \"Wallet\", \"Alerts\", and \"Settings\" tabs. I am sketching out interactive modals for boarding pass displays, trip detail additions, and wallet views. I\'m also visualizing an alerts view with live notification simulations and settings views to toggle preferences. I am working to define these interactive elements to enable a clean, logical user journey. I am also working on Gemini AI integration with an express backend.\n\n\n**Refining Backend Logic**\n\nI\'m now integrating AI for trip parsing. I\'m focusing on the `parse-trip` function, which now takes confirmation emails or flight codes, extracts structured JSON using Gemini, and returns it for itinerary building. I\'ve also added an `/api/flight-status` endpoint for real-time data. Furthermore, I\'ve checked and updated the `package.json` scripts to support the Express server in development and esbuild for building, as suggested in the full-stack guidelines. I\'ve ensured the correct fonts are loaded in the `index.html` to be sure the icons are rendered correctly.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 334578123
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
