  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Weather Widget**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing a dedicated destination weather widget or card component for the timeline. The goal is to make it visually clear and concise, integrating seamlessly into the existing timeline structure. This involves considering the best way to display the current weather and a 3-day forecast, optimizing for both aesthetics and efficient information delivery.\n\n\n**Defining Weather Data Requirements**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the exact data points required for the destination weather card. I\'ve broken it down: location details (name, code) and the weather data itself. I\'m exploring an API to fetch this live data, considering Open-Meteo as a free and reliable option, suggesting a server endpoint to simplify integration.\n\n\n**Implementing Weather API Endpoint**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `/api/weather` endpoint in `server.ts`. The focus is on handling city or airport code queries, resolving airport codes to city names, and querying the Open-Meteo API. I\'m mapping WMO weather codes to human-readable conditions and Material symbol icons for visual clarity. I\'m also planning integration and testing with the timeline.\n\n\n**Defining Weather Card Content**\n\nI\'m now detailing the specific content for the destination weather card, focusing on New York (JFK). I\'m planning to include a \"Live Weather API\" badge, current temperature with condition, a 3-day forecast, and interactive elements. The plan is to include Fahrenheit/Celsius toggling, a refresh feature, and tap-to-expand details. I\'m prioritizing building the `/api/weather` route in `server.ts` to ensure reliable data fetching.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 780410627
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
